  "description": "The certification regarding lobbying for contracts, grants, loans and cooperative agreements, with the statement for loan guarantees and loan insurance. The applicant names its organization and authorized representative; Grants.gov fills in the signature and date.",
  "notes": [
    "SGG already has this form (`gg_lobbying_form`). The definition uses its property names and sections, so a draft saved on the existing form reads the same.",
    "The certification and the loan statement are quoted exactly from the DAT as the first section's description, with the loan statement's heading in bold.",
    "Grants.gov copies the organization, name and title from the SF-424. The API has no rule that does that, so the applicant enters them, as on SGG's existing form.",
    "Signature and Submitted Date are filled in by the API on submission (`gg_post_population` rules `signature` and `current_date`), so the form shows them read-only.",
    "Labels are those of SGG's existing form. Standardizing them on the question bank's labels comes later."
  ],
